WEBVTT

00:00:00.970 --> 00:00:04.300
This is Technical Sergeant
Liliko Kinutsugai from Misawa Air Base.

00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:05.930
Her TAC name is Jimmy.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.560
Next is Technical Sergeant Mayumi Hitomi
from Iruma Air Base.

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:11.060
Goes by the TAC name Morris.

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:15.310
Lastly, from Tsuiki Air Base is
Senior Master Sergeant El Hoshino.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.150
Her TAC name is Penguin.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:21.690
These three OTF pilots
will be joining us for training.

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:22.990
Joint training?

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.740
The training will also focus
on OTF stress relief.

00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:30.160
-We'll hold a realistic mock battle...
-Seriously? Three more?

00:00:30.290 --> 00:00:32.210
And Dragon Pilots are all women, too.

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:33.410
Jackpot!

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.670
-Harem status!
-What are you so happy about?

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:39.920
Do you know how much we've suffered
from that woman?

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.050
I'm informed that all three women
have exceptional piloting skills,

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:47.140
incomparable to our own
Technical Sergeant Hisone Amakasu.

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.930
When you phrase it like that,
it's not exactly uplifting...

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:52.930
Dragon Pilots are all the same!

00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:54.730
Skilled or not!

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:56.190
Now, now.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:58.270
If Dragon Pilots come from other bases,

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.860
then Technical Sergeant Amakasu
would represent Gifu.

00:01:01.990 --> 00:01:03.240
Represent?

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:04.860
Exactly!

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:09.160
Flight Leader Kogure
just mentioned something great!

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:13.330
As the Gifu Air Base representative,
in other words, as the face of Gifu,

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:16.210
-She's talking about the show!
-...to prove Gifu's potential,

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.000
I will give it my all!

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:09.030
What's with those names, Jimmy and Morris?

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.570
And Penguin sounds so weak.

00:03:11.950 --> 00:03:14.950
But even Amakasu has a TAC name...

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.910
What the hell!

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.000
In my case, I would be...

00:03:20.540 --> 00:03:23.000
Sexy...

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.250
Jaguar!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:28.630
Maybe not.

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:30.220
-There it is.
-Huh?

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.800
Yeah, yeah. That's right, that's right.

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:34.390
True, true.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:36.810
-Amakasu.
-Ah! Nao!

00:03:36.890 --> 00:03:37.930
What are you doing?

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:41.230
The bathroom is supposed to be
the one inviolable place of privacy!

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.770
It's only because you were
muttering nonstop.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:44.860
What're you reading?

00:03:45.690 --> 00:03:46.690
This.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:48.820
How to be empathetic?

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:52.490
Personal relations are
what I avoid the most!

00:03:52.910 --> 00:03:55.030
To fulfill my role as the face of Gifu

00:03:55.120 --> 00:03:59.290
and work well with the other pilots,
I should learn from my predecessors!

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.750
-By reading this sketchy article?
-Exactly.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:05.460
For you, who lives
by your beastly intuition,

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:08.710
you might not even need
a TAC name like "Sexy Jaguar."

00:04:09.300 --> 00:04:10.260
Ow!

00:04:10.970 --> 00:04:13.180
I realized at the air show the other day

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:17.050
that I must possess
the talent to be a Dragon Pilot!

00:04:17.140 --> 00:04:17.970
Huh?

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:22.640
Which is even more of a reason
not to let personal relations stop me!

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:24.850
Every word she says pisses me off.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:27.400
Yup. True, true.

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:29.280
Just like you said, Sexy Jaguar!

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:30.740
Ow! Ouch!

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:33.200
That really hurts, Nao!

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.950
You two! Hurry and meet at the apron!

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:37.950
Huh?

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:41.910
It seems all three OTF are arriving
at the same time.

00:04:42.620 --> 00:04:45.000
<i>Runway 28, continue approach.</i>

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.340
<i>Runway 28, cleared to land.</i>

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:49.500
<i>Wind 140 at 8.</i>

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:50.630
Norell 01.

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:51.880
Roger.

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:53.380
Cleared to land.

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:42.140
This'll be quite the spectacle.

00:05:42.220 --> 00:05:43.180
Yeah.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.690
They're about ready to come out.

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:56.110
Sniff, sniff.

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.740
Munch. Gulp.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:03.200
Even the Gifu air tastes good, Futomomo.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:20.430
Uh, please don't look this way.
Staring triggers my ophthalmophobia.

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:22.390
These are the Dragon Pilots?

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:23.970
They're pretty faint of heart.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.270
And they're not all slimy.

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:27.230
Slimy?

00:06:27.770 --> 00:06:30.350
Why doesn't F-2 change into Hotel mode?

00:06:42.620 --> 00:06:43.620
Nice to meet you.

00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:46.200
I am El Hoshino from Tsuiki Air Base.

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.710
I look forward to receiving
your encouragement and guidance.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.500
And this one here...

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:53.090
Is an overachiever.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.380
She's not slimy, either!

00:06:55.460 --> 00:06:57.170
A properly trained pilot

00:06:57.260 --> 00:07:00.760
does not needlessly
stimluate the OTC's insides.

00:07:01.340 --> 00:07:03.350
All right, time to take a run.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:04.260
Right now?

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:07.270
You're not exempt
just because you arrived now.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:09.140
This is how we do things at Gifu!

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:10.600
Isn't that right, Amakasu?

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:11.520
Yes, sir!

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:13.400
Time to empathize!

00:07:15.980 --> 00:07:18.190
Hey! Pick up the pace!

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:20.490
If you want to be
on the same playing field,

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:22.700
you gotta be twice as tough as the boys!

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:29.960
I can't do it. My body feels so heavy.

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:31.460
Of course, of course!

00:07:32.290 --> 00:07:35.840
I really am just a useless human,
dragging my feet.

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:38.050
I see, I see!

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:40.220
Oh?

00:07:40.550 --> 00:07:44.010
You're completely missing
the point of empathy.

00:07:45.970 --> 00:07:47.770
This is where you will stay.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:51.440
Ah, a room for six.

00:07:52.310 --> 00:07:53.440
What're ya doing?

00:07:53.600 --> 00:07:55.480
Ensuring my personal space.

00:07:55.770 --> 00:07:56.610
Hey,

00:07:57.570 --> 00:08:00.860
-wanna do flight training now?
-What? Right now?

00:08:01.570 --> 00:08:03.780
I've received permission
from the commander.

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:08.080
We should do everything we can to learn
about each others' OTF's capabilities.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:09.950
I'll pass.

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.250
I wish not to exert too much energy.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:17.920
My Futomomo had to fly so far from Iruma.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.880
-I want to give him time to rest--
-Are you being serious?

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:22.220
Oh?

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.390
We've taken the maintenance team
away from their normal duties.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:30.640
Seeing that should make you realize
exactly how vital this joint training is.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.190
We have to bring results to satisfy
their high expectations too.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:36.060
-We are--
-You're right!

00:08:36.150 --> 00:08:37.230
As the face of Gifu--

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:39.110
What's with you suddenly?

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:40.650
Hoshino's remarks...

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:42.860
are true words of empathy!

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:46.280
Pure empathy
without a shred of dishonesty.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:47.450
So what?

00:08:47.780 --> 00:08:49.370
Are you gonna do it or not?

00:08:49.660 --> 00:08:51.660
Of course I'm doing it!

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.830
Well then. You show promise.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:56.250
Empathy.

00:09:01.050 --> 00:09:05.300
-Looks like they're going on a flight.
-Yeah. They just decided the plan.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:08.180
But Tsuiki's OTF sure is amazing.

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.600
Even when it's off duty,
it maintains Foxtrot mode.

00:09:11.770 --> 00:09:16.230
Well, it's been like that ever since
Hoshino became a Dragon Pilot.

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:17.520
What's wrong?

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:19.020
You can relax a little.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:23.690
Your OTF is just rearing to go,
isn't it, Hoshino?

00:09:23.780 --> 00:09:24.610
Amakasu.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:27.070
Is there something wrong with my F-2?

00:09:27.160 --> 00:09:29.740
No, but I wanted to make adjustments
before the flight--

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:30.660
It's unnecessary.

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:35.710
But staying in the fitted equipment
for an extended time can stress the--

00:09:35.790 --> 00:09:37.370
My F-2 is a fighter jet.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:40.630
I don't need you to treat it like a pet.

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:43.170
-Question!
-Yes, Amakasu.

00:09:43.420 --> 00:09:48.510
Then will you let the face of Gifu...
no, Masotan and I show you how we fly?

00:09:49.260 --> 00:09:50.100
Huh?

00:09:52.930 --> 00:09:54.140
<i>Mambo Viking 01.</i>

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:57.310
<i>Wind 080 at 6.</i>

00:09:57.390 --> 00:09:58.650
<i>Cleared for takeoff.</i>

00:09:59.020 --> 00:10:04.150
Masotan, we're already in league with
tremendous, high-performance elites!

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:06.650
Let's show Hoshino what we're made of!

00:10:19.330 --> 00:10:21.290
Yes, I understand.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:22.550
Bye.

00:10:25.210 --> 00:10:28.550
It's rare for him
to personally make a visit here.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:33.220
Well, this joint training was his idea
in the first place.

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:37.060
In any case,
each woman is very individualistic.

00:10:37.230 --> 00:10:38.060
On the surface.

00:10:38.890 --> 00:10:44.320
But oddly enough,
the OTF sniffed them out...

00:10:49.660 --> 00:10:54.950
by the one thing connecting
all of the chosen women.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:58.370
-What was that?
-They're all over the place.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:00.880
Because of people like that...

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:05.590
Hiso Maso!

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:09.180
PLEASE KEEP THE RESTROOM CLEAN

00:11:12.510 --> 00:11:13.970
Thanks.

00:11:14.050 --> 00:11:18.270
Being shaken in every way possible
would make anyone like this...

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:20.980
Once you recover, wanna go for a drink?

00:11:21.060 --> 00:11:24.190
Why would you invite someone
who was puking her guts out for a drink?

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:26.320
Only a real airhead would do that--

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:27.780
Hoshino!

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:31.070
-What'll you do?
-Of course I'll go!

00:11:31.200 --> 00:11:34.280
Is that so? I'll go ask the others too.

00:11:38.410 --> 00:11:40.210
Amakasu, are you still alive?

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:41.670
Drinkommunication!

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:45.920
With the power of alcohol,
we can close the gap!

00:11:50.340 --> 00:11:51.930
So his name is Masotan!

00:11:52.590 --> 00:11:55.680
The "Sota" in his name is adorable.

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:59.640
You call your OTF "Futomomo," right?

00:11:59.850 --> 00:12:01.270
Yes, I do.

00:12:01.810 --> 00:12:04.610
Because his thighs
are his most charming assets.

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:08.030
It makes him so happy
when I pet him there.

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:08.980
I... see...

00:12:09.070 --> 00:12:12.820
My TAC name was taken from Futomomo too.

00:12:12.910 --> 00:12:15.910
I'm Morris because Futomomo gives me
more and more.

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:17.280
What about your OTF?

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:19.540
My OTF's name is Akemi.

00:12:19.700 --> 00:12:22.540
My TAC name is Jimmy
since it's plain and boring like me.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:26.590
That's not true at all.
Or maybe just a little?

00:12:26.670 --> 00:12:29.800
You don't need to sugarcoat it.
In the first place...

00:12:29.880 --> 00:12:34.050
<i>Oh my gosh! We're actually</i>
<i>engaging in girl talk!</i>

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:35.300
<i>At this rate,</i>

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:39.600
<i>I might actually make friends</i>
<i>for the first time in my life!</i>

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:41.730
Hoshino.

00:12:42.310 --> 00:12:44.310
What's your OTF's name?

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:45.350
F-2.

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:48.070
Oh, I didn't mean the plane equipment--

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:49.610
All of you...

00:12:49.860 --> 00:12:51.860
think too little
of your positions as pilots.

00:12:52.780 --> 00:12:56.570
This is not a zoo
and we are not zookeepers.

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:01.660
We are pilots and OTF belong to the base.
There's no need for names.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:03.370
Don't you get that?

00:13:04.790 --> 00:13:06.460
B-But Hoshino,

00:13:06.670 --> 00:13:08.670
you've got a cute TAC name.

00:13:10.170 --> 00:13:14.340
The first fearless penguin in the group
to jump into the ocean.

00:13:15.090 --> 00:13:16.470
That's where it came from.

00:13:17.430 --> 00:13:21.140
I will become...
the first female fighter pilot.

00:13:21.810 --> 00:13:23.100
First penguin.

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:27.440
I don't sense that fighting spirit
in any of you.

00:13:27.900 --> 00:13:33.110
Well... since we fly dragons
and not fighter jets...

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:35.610
How should I put it so you understand?

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:39.370
Because you view your OTF as dragons,

00:13:39.450 --> 00:13:41.370
you're all no good.

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:42.700
M-Me?

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:44.040
The rest of you too.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:46.290
Your OTF are slacking off.

00:13:46.540 --> 00:13:49.460
Dragon Pilots on the whole
are looked down upon because of you--

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:50.380
Pardon me,

00:13:50.750 --> 00:13:53.630
I'm aware that I am no good,

00:13:53.800 --> 00:13:57.010
but Futomomo is trying his hardest.

00:13:57.590 --> 00:14:00.260
He never slacks off.

00:14:02.890 --> 00:14:04.890
So you're a zookeeper?

00:14:05.180 --> 00:14:06.020
In that case,

00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:09.480
think of how to tame your animal.

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:13.610
Come on, don't say that!

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:18.030
Yeah, but tomorrow's the mock battle.
I don't think we should drink.

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.080
Hey! You there!

00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.750
If I remember correctly...

00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:25.750
El, right?

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:26.660
Yeah.

00:14:26.870 --> 00:14:29.120
Oh, so you were drinking?

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:31.840
Wanna go back in for another round?

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.670
-But--
-We should strengthen our camaraderie.

00:14:34.760 --> 00:14:37.880
Especially since I'll be
the aggressor tomorrow.

00:14:38.590 --> 00:14:39.430
Huh?

00:14:40.140 --> 00:14:43.510
I didn't come to Gifu
to play games and make friends.

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:45.140
If you'll excuse me.

00:14:47.140 --> 00:14:49.140
Z-Zaito?

00:14:49.350 --> 00:14:53.570
Do you know the strategy...
for capturing prideful women?

00:14:53.860 --> 00:14:54.690
What?

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:57.150
Once you've pierced a hole in their armor,

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:59.950
just keep beating through
till you wear them down!

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:03.240
It's settled!
This is no time for drinking.

00:15:03.330 --> 00:15:04.540
I'm gonna hit the gym.

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:05.540
See ya!

00:15:05.830 --> 00:15:06.750
Woo hoo!

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:08.960
He's frightening in more ways than one...

00:15:12.040 --> 00:15:14.040
I will now begin the briefing.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:17.090
Amakasu! Explain the conditions
for training completion.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:18.170
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:24.390
Hitomi's transport and Kinutsugai's AWACS
aircraft are to avoid being shot down,

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:28.930
while Hoshino and my fighter jets
will escort them to ensure safe passage.

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:33.190
Good! HAVCAP must make instant decisions,
so cooperation is vital!

00:15:33.730 --> 00:15:35.690
Zaito and Onaga will be the aggressors!

00:15:36.110 --> 00:15:38.610
Sorry, but I'm not gonna hold back.

00:15:38.940 --> 00:15:41.700
If you don't,
the mock battle would be obsolete.

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:44.910
Wahoo! I'm getting all fired up dammit!

00:15:44.990 --> 00:15:45.910
Shut the hell up!

00:16:00.760 --> 00:16:01.590
Listen up.

00:16:01.840 --> 00:16:04.390
Maintain formation
and proceed slowly as planned.

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:05.850
Yes, sir.

00:16:05.930 --> 00:16:08.220
I should stay out of Hoshino's way.

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:12.690
I'm not Hitomi, but I don't want someone
badmouthing Masotan either.

00:16:17.360 --> 00:16:18.400
<i>Are you ready, Long?</i>

00:16:18.820 --> 00:16:21.700
<i>Attack on sight. No holding back!</i>

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:22.650
<i>You got it!</i>

00:16:24.280 --> 00:16:26.700
Contact. Compass 320.

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.200
Distance at 26 miles.

00:16:28.330 --> 00:16:31.460
Elevation at 30,000.
Eagle, two aircraft. Hostile.

00:16:32.210 --> 00:16:33.210
Already?

00:16:33.290 --> 00:16:35.080
<i>Shall we change course?</i>

00:16:35.170 --> 00:16:36.790
What should we do, Hoshino?

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:38.840
<i>What?</i>

00:16:42.720 --> 00:16:44.010
I'll draw the enemy away.

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:44.930
<i>What?</i>

00:16:45.010 --> 00:16:47.550
<i>You three maintain formation</i>
<i>and proceed as normal!</i>

00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:48.760
Hoshino!

00:16:49.260 --> 00:16:51.060
Taking off on her own...

00:16:51.140 --> 00:16:53.310
Let's just see what happens
for the time being.

00:16:53.730 --> 00:16:56.690
-What are you--
-The main purpose of this mock battle

00:16:57.060 --> 00:17:00.980
is to let the Dragon Pilots take action
to achieve their goal.

00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:02.990
Tally-ho!

00:17:03.450 --> 00:17:05.240
They're coming to greet us?

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:07.660
They're really making it fun for us.

00:17:07.740 --> 00:17:10.370
<i>Are you really going to beat through them?</i>

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:11.580
Of course!

00:17:11.700 --> 00:17:13.500
<i>I'll tear their pride to shreds,</i>

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:17.500
<i>and when they compromise,</i>
<i>that's when it's fever time!</i>

00:17:42.070 --> 00:17:44.240
<i>Let's distance ourselves</i>
<i>from them while we can.</i>

00:17:44.320 --> 00:17:45.150
<i>Okay!</i>

00:18:13.100 --> 00:18:15.140
I will not lose.

00:18:15.230 --> 00:18:18.150
<i>From other Dragon Pilots</i>
<i>or any other pilot!</i>

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:21.980
And I will show you all...
that I will become...

00:18:22.570 --> 00:18:23.730
the first penguin!

00:18:26.070 --> 00:18:27.320
-What?
-Huh?

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:30.660
-What's wrong, Hoshino?
-<i>I'm fine!</i>

00:18:30.740 --> 00:18:32.160
Fine, my ass!

00:18:32.280 --> 00:18:33.790
Tell me what's happening!

00:18:33.870 --> 00:18:35.870
<i>I said I'm fine!</i>

00:18:35.950 --> 00:18:37.830
-Hey, Hoshino!
-Flight Leader Maezawa!

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:40.830
Senior Master Sergeant Hoshino's
OTF's tail is exposed!

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:41.960
What?

00:18:42.130 --> 00:18:43.960
<i>Hoshino, return to base immediately!</i>

00:18:44.050 --> 00:18:46.550
-No!
-<i>You're entering a golf course air field!</i>

00:18:46.630 --> 00:18:49.090
-<i>If a civilian sees you--</i>
-I'll figure it out!

00:18:49.180 --> 00:18:50.340
<i>You idiot!</i>

00:18:50.430 --> 00:18:51.680
<i>That's an order!</i>

00:18:51.930 --> 00:18:52.890
<i>Hoshino!</i>

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:54.680
-<i>Are you listening to me?</i>
<i>-</i>No...

00:18:55.390 --> 00:18:56.220
No!

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.190
Not here... not now...

00:18:58.310 --> 00:18:59.520
<i>Hoshino!</i>

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:02.190
No!!

00:19:34.140 --> 00:19:36.520
I understand what she wanted.

00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:37.520
But...

00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.850
to think she'd have to go this far...

00:19:41.440 --> 00:19:42.730
Why didn't you stop her?

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:44.270
M-Maezawa, please...

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:45.480
You knew...

00:19:45.570 --> 00:19:47.570
that Hoshino's F-2 had a problem!

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:50.490
And you still let her do
the joint training!

00:19:54.120 --> 00:19:54.950
Um...

00:19:55.370 --> 00:19:56.370
The worst...

00:19:56.450 --> 00:19:57.290
What?

00:19:57.370 --> 00:19:58.500
This is the worst!

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.790
It was just an animal after all.

00:20:03.790 --> 00:20:06.880
It ignored my orders
and transformed on its own!

00:20:07.960 --> 00:20:09.380
I am a pilot!

00:20:09.760 --> 00:20:11.630
-I'm not a zookeeper!
-W-Wait...

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.890
I don't need a piece of junk like that!

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:18.600
Oh, um...

00:20:18.720 --> 00:20:20.730
How should I put this...

00:20:23.060 --> 00:20:24.690
Well...

00:20:25.650 --> 00:20:28.610
Dragons... are not things.

00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:32.900
Wipe, wipe.

00:20:33.860 --> 00:20:36.580
Grab, grab. Hurry, hurry.

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:41.620
W-What... What's with her?

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:45.000
It's true that they shouldn't be treated
as things.

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:46.170
Huh?

00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:49.920
Besides, the shortcomings of an F-2
lies with the Dragon Pilot.

00:20:50.090 --> 00:20:53.510
If you call F-2 a piece of junk,
then you're a piece of junk too!

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:57.050
I understand well the desire
to turn away from reality,

00:20:57.140 --> 00:21:00.020
But that only delays
facing the real problem--

00:21:02.430 --> 00:21:03.890
I was just joking!

00:21:03.980 --> 00:21:04.980
Uh...

00:21:05.060 --> 00:21:07.400
You had a valid point too.

00:21:07.900 --> 00:21:09.730
You're mocking me, aren't you?

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:10.860
True, true.

00:21:15.910 --> 00:21:16.990
Wait!

00:21:21.200 --> 00:21:23.040
And then, there was no one.

00:21:23.410 --> 00:21:24.580
Kinutsugai?

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:28.630
I will be gone in a minute as well.
I want to use the bathroom.

00:21:29.500 --> 00:21:32.260
By the way, that was pretty bad.

00:21:33.220 --> 00:21:35.050
What you said to Hoshino

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:38.470
would be enough to make me want to die.

00:21:38.550 --> 00:21:40.760
I was just trying to get along
with every--

00:21:40.850 --> 00:21:43.350
Oh. I'm 20 seconds overdue.

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.560
I would certainly die
if I peed myself here.

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:47.730
Farewell.

00:21:53.320 --> 00:21:55.150
I... I...

00:21:56.280 --> 00:21:57.110
I am...

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:00.580
the absolute worst!!

00:22:03.370 --> 00:22:04.540
This is the best.

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:09.670
I can say it's actually
a better development.

00:22:09.960 --> 00:22:12.630
Vice-Minister Iiboshi, in that case--

00:22:12.750 --> 00:22:16.930
Yes. We cannot let
such a good opportunity slip away.

00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:22.600
We must turn our attention to the future
government and get to the bottom of it.

00:22:23.600 --> 00:22:26.480
Τhe true connection between OTF and pilot.

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:31.650
The OTF acknowledge only one point
of commonality in those girls.

00:22:34.440 --> 00:22:35.900
White Lover.

00:22:36.190 --> 00:22:38.990
TO BE CONTINUED

00:24:09.870 --> 00:24:13.790
-Nothing, nothing, there's nothing here.
-What are you doing!

00:24:13.880 --> 00:24:15.920
Bam bada bam bada bam bam...

00:24:16.000 --> 00:24:17.300
Fever, fever!

00:24:17.380 --> 00:24:19.300
Everyone is mocking me.

00:24:19.380 --> 00:24:21.090
They're trying to cheer you up!

00:24:21.170 --> 00:24:22.470
That's a lie.
